        "q": "Why does ReadRecordsResponse.pageToken come back as an empty string instead of null?",
        "a": "Because some versions return it that way. Google's read guide notes that depending on the system or Health Connect APK version, such as on Android 12 and 13 or across specific IPC serialization boundaries, pageToken can be an empty string instead of null when pagination is complete. Google's advice is to check with isNullOrEmpty() rather than only for null, even though the reference itself still describes null as the end-of-pages value."
