        "q": "Does TimeRangeFilter.between include a record that starts exactly at the end time?",
        "a": "No. Google's TimeRangeFilter reference describes between as inclusive-exclusive: a record at the start time is included and one at the end time is not. The before form treats its end time as exclusive and the after form treats its start time as inclusive. Adjacent windows built this way, such as midnight to midnight, therefore do not share a boundary instant."
